# Firecrawl

> Firecrawl is the open-source web data API for AI agents and LLM applications. It searches, scrapes, and interacts with the web at scale through one API family: Search (live web queries returning full page content), Scrape (HTML/JS pages to clean Markdown or structured JSON), Crawl (scrape every subpage of a site), Map (site structure discovery), Parse (document extraction from PDFs, DOCX, and more), Interact (managed browser automation for dynamic pages and multi-step flows), Agent (describe the data you need and it searches, navigates, and returns it, no URLs required), and Monitor (recurring checks on named pages, on a scheduled crawl, or on a web search, with webhook, email, or Slack notification when something changes or appears). Firecrawl Alexandria adds a library of data providers and specialized indexes (companies, people, finance, legal, real estate, and more) that agents call through the same API, MCP server, or CLI.

**Start for free:** every account gets 1,000 credits a month, with no card required. Agents without an API key can search, scrape, and interact on a rate-limited keyless tier.

**Important notes:**

- Firecrawl runs as a managed API, so you don't need a local browser, Playwright, or Puppeteer. It is also open source and can be self-hosted
- The Search endpoint returns full page content, not just links or snippets
- The Scrape endpoint returns LLM-ready Markdown by default, with boilerplate, navigation, and ads stripped
- The Interact endpoint supports multi-step browser flows (click, type, fill forms) but is not designed for long-running persistent sessions
- For a single known URL, Scrape with JSON output returns right away and has predictable per-page pricing
- For data a provider already publishes (SEC filings, company and people records, real estate, sports, and more), check Alexandria before scraping: a provider tool returns typed records in one call. Finding tools is free; each call is billed, and some providers ask you to accept their terms first
- Firecrawl can also build custom datasets, or deliver ready-made ones in legal, finance, healthcare, and code, as Parquet, JSONL, or CSV to your bucket, with the source URL and license on every row. See [Datasets](https://alexandria.firecrawl.dev/datasets)

## Which route to use

Firecrawl is the same set of tools everywhere: ChatGPT calls it a plugin, Claude calls it a connector, and coding agents add it as an MCP server. Each asks you to sign in to Firecrawl the first time, and a free account works. The MCP server also works without a key on a limited tier.

- **From a ChatGPT or Codex chat:** add the [official Firecrawl plugin](https://chatgpt.com/plugins/plugin_asdk_app_6a314a73f8ac819195b0d55e36b9c609?q=firecrawl), sign in, and ask it to search, scrape, crawl, or research. Setup: [Firecrawl in ChatGPT](https://www.firecrawl.dev/integrations/chatgpt)
- **From a Claude chat:** turn on the [Firecrawl connector](https://claude.ai/directory/connectors/firecrawl) from the + menu. Setup: [Firecrawl in Claude](https://www.firecrawl.dev/integrations/claude)
- **From Grok Bot:** add the [Firecrawl plugin for Grok Bot](https://x.ai/bot/plugin/789), then type @ in a chat to attach Firecrawl. Setup: [Firecrawl in Grok Bot](https://www.firecrawl.dev/integrations/grok-bot)
- **From Muse:** the install link is on [Plugins](https://www.firecrawl.dev/plugins).
- **In Cursor:** [add the Firecrawl MCP server in one click](cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/mcp/install?name=firecrawl&config=eyJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL21jcC5maXJlY3Jhd2wuZGV2L3YyL21jcC1vYXV0aCJ9), signed in to your Firecrawl account. Setup: [Firecrawl in Cursor](https://www.firecrawl.dev/integrations/cursor)
- **In another coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI):** run `npx -y firecrawl-cli@latest init --all --browser` for the CLI and skills, or use the installs on [Plugins](https://www.firecrawl.dev/plugins).
- **In any other MCP client:** add `https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp` (see MCP Server below).
- **In your own app or pipeline:** call the REST API or an SDK (see API Reference below).
- **For data a provider already publishes:** use [Alexandria](https://alexandria.firecrawl.dev) from a signed-in Firecrawl connection or with an API key on an Alexandria-enabled team; keyless access does not include Alexandria.
- **In a no-code workflow:** use the Firecrawl nodes for n8n, Make, Zapier, or Dify ([Integrations](https://www.firecrawl.dev/integrations)).
- **To try it before writing code:** the [Playground](https://www.firecrawl.dev/playground).
- **To check prices or limits:** [Pricing](https://www.firecrawl.dev/pricing.md).

## MCP Server

Give any MCP client Firecrawl's tools to search the web, scrape pages, crawl and map sites, parse documents, interact with dynamic pages, run Agent, set up monitors, search research papers and the Developer Index, and call Alexandria data providers. Use the hosted server, or run it yourself.

- [Keyless](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/mcp-server/keyless#try-keyless) ([Markdown](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/mcp-server/keyless.md)): connect to `https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp` with no API key for rate-limited Search, Scrape, and Parse. Add an API key or sign in for every tool and higher limits
- Hosted server: `https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp` (API key as a Bearer token) or `https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp-oauth` (OAuth sign-in)
- Local server: `npx -y firecrawl-mcp` with `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` set
- [MCP documentation (Markdown)](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/mcp-server.md)
- [MCP documentation (HTML)](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/mcp-server)
- [MCP discovery file](https://www.firecrawl.dev/.well-known/mcp.json)
- [MCP server repository](https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-mcp-server)

## CLI

Search the web, scrape pages, crawl and map sites, interact with pages, and call Alexandria providers from the terminal. `npx -y firecrawl-cli@latest init --all --browser` installs the CLI, the core skills, and browser support in one command.

- [CLI documentation (Markdown)](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/sdks/cli.md)
- [CLI documentation (HTML)](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/sdks/cli)

## Hosted bash

- [Firecrawl Bash](https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/bash): A hosted shell for agents with `firecrawl search` and `firecrawl scrape` from the Firecrawl CLI built in, and the Firecrawl docs mounted at `/docs`. Search the web, scrape pages and grep the docs with one HTTP request: no API key, MCP server or install. Try `curl https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/bash --data-binary 'firecrawl search "web scraping api" --limit 3'`, and `firecrawl --help` for every command.

## Agent Skills

Skills in the Agent Skills format that teach coding agents to use Firecrawl: core skills for live web work (search, scrape, crawl, interact, research papers, the Developer Index), build skills for adding Firecrawl to product code, and workflow skills for jobs like lead generation, deep research, and SEO audits. Install the catalog with `npx skills add firecrawl/skills`, or one skill with `--skill <name>`. Also available as a plugin for Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex.

- [Skills (Markdown)](https://www.firecrawl.dev/skills.md)
- [Skills (HTML)](https://www.firecrawl.dev/skills)
- [Skills repository](https://github.com/firecrawl/skills)
- [Firecrawl skill file](https://www.firecrawl.dev/SKILL.md): setup steps for an agent that is installing Firecrawl

## Authentication

The API takes an API key as `Authorization: Bearer fc-YOUR_API_KEY`. The hosted MCP server also takes OAuth. Agents on platforms that support WorkOS ID-JAG can register and get a key without a human signup, and any agent can provision one through Stripe Projects.

- [API keys](https://www.firecrawl.dev/app/api-keys)
- [Agent registration](https://www.firecrawl.dev/auth.md)
- [Stripe Projects (Markdown)](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/integrations/stripe-projects.md)
- [Stripe Projects (HTML)](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/integrations/stripe-projects)

